{
  "rationale": "Use a minimal plant split into sensing and motion capability, then encode the exploration policy in small deterministic specifications. The policy prioritizes forward progress in clear space, uses directed one-shot turns for side obstacles, uses a brief backward escape only after front obstacles, and returns to forward exploration immediately on path_clear. Action states self-loop on path_clear so open-loop pulses are not unnecessarily preempted, while obstacle events force recovery transitions for safety.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate uncontrollable perception from controllable motion capability with two plant automata",
    "Use one policy specification to map sensed conditions to exactly one allowed action per decision/recovery state while keeping all uncontrollable events total",
    "Bias clear-space behavior to move_forward, reserve random_walk and full_rotate by disabling them in the policy, and use move_backward only as a one-shot front-obstacle escape"
  ],
